@@ -550,3 +550,13 @@ capabilities and operation actions. Access requires a verified service token
 and an explicit Nova service-user allowlist, in addition to project policy.
 New checkpoint creation is disabled by default. This private version does
 not assert compatibility with an upstream OpenStack microversion.
+
+3.73 (private fork extension)
+-----------------------------
+
+Adds explicit service continuation to the initial dual-identity checkpoint
+reservation. The original actor and owner remain immutable. Dedicated routes
+allow the authenticated service subject to continue only its delegated
+operation, subject to the service role, allowlist, policy and durable grant.
+Service-only credentials cannot reserve a new operation. Released grants are
+read-only tombstones. Existing 3.72 request and response semantics remain.
